tman trailer is 100  feral meckler wrote immediately texted  matson tomlin to make sure cause i  couldn't believe it  it's him all right as it is farrell's  prosthetic heavy appearance in the  batman trailer means the character may  be far more of an unknown quantity than  expected that's likely a good thing as  the footage for the batman paints reeves  new batflick as more of a grounded  noir-tinged tale of hero vs villains  meaning a more comic faithful adaptation  of the penguin would feel extremely out  of place  in a recent interview with gma news  farrell also teased we'll be seeing less  of his character in the villain pack the  batman than previously thought  he shared i haven't got that much to do  i'm not all over it by any means  it seems that farrell's two blink and  you miss him scenes in the batman's  teaser trailer may represent the bulk of  his screen time for the film  happily though the actor went on to note  he still got a few choice moments with  mr vengeance in the batman  he dished there are a couple of some  tasty scenes i haven't into my creation  and i can't wait to get back  it feels original and fun but i'm only  at the start of the journey so i can't  wait to get back and really get into it  that start of the journey tease may not  sound like much but with barrel  apparently  playing second fiddle to the riddler and  the batman it could mean his penguin is  setting up to feature predominantly in a  batman sequel  the batman is set for release on october  1st 2021  the film also stars andy circus as  alfred pennyworth the wayne family's  faithful butler and bruce's most trusted  confidant  john turturro is mob boss and batman  enemy carmine palcone  peter skarsgard as district attorney gil  coulson and jamie lawson as mayoral  candidate bella real  as well as charlie carver max carver and  gil perez abraham in undisclosed roles  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

